WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:01.829
Accidents will happen.

00:00:01.829 --> 00:00:04.570
But once in awhile, they're blessings in disguise.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:08.920
Take TV show bloopers: sometimes they make
the show funnier, more convincing, or just

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.680
more all-around interesting.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.850
These bloopers from popular TV shows were
just so perfect for the plot and characters,

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.830
they had to stay in the final cut.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:18.830
Seinfeld

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:23.580
The best Seinfeld episodes featured the fabulous
foursome struggling with some kind of existential

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.580
nightmare.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.980
Perhaps the best example is the 1991 episode
"The Parking Garage," in which the gang spends

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.059
the entire story wandering around a parking
complex, unable to find their car until the

00:00:33.059 --> 00:00:34.059
very end.

00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:37.969
As scripted, the episode was supposed to finish
with some small talk and the group driving

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:40.039
off, their struggle final over.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:44.249
But when actor Michael Richards put the key
in the ignition, the car wouldn't start — an

00:00:44.249 --> 00:00:47.120
unplanned ending that cracked up the cast
and crew.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.030
It's a more fitting and funnier way to wrap
up the story, and it proved just too good

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.510
to cut.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:00:59.889
Supernatural

00:00:59.889 --> 00:01:04.869
A commonly uttered profane phrase doubled
as an catchphrase for paranormal investigator

00:01:04.869 --> 00:01:07.090
Dean Winchester on Supernatural.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:11.299
Actor Jensen Ackles uttered the line as an
off-script addition while making the 2007

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.170
episode "Bad Day at Black Rock."

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.920
"Son of a bitch!"

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:22.360
His boisterous, hilariously frustrated, over-the-top
delivery did a number on costar Jared Padalecki,

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:26.960
and the inspired improvisation made it into
the final episode.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.200
Friends

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:33.659
Ross Geller was always a man with quirky pursuits—like
playing experimental keyboard music and owning

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:35.010
a monkey, for example.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:39.570
In the seventh-season Friends episode "The
One With Joey's New Brain," Ross desperately

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:44.000
wants to play the bagpipes at Chandler and
Monica's upcoming wedding…even though they

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.359
aren't interested, and despite his complete
inability to actually play the instrument.

00:01:48.359 --> 00:01:53.100
During a sneak peek, actress Jennifer Aniston
clearly can't handle it, and does everything

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:57.530
in her power to not break — a real-life
reaction too good to leave on the cutting-room

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.060
floor.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.619
How I Met Your Mother

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:05.149
Wayne Brady's first big claim to fame was
as a gifted improvisational comic on ABC's

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:06.670
Whose Line is It Anyway?

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:10.471
In Brady's first episode as Barney's brother
on the sitcom How I Met Your Mother, actor

00:02:10.471 --> 00:02:15.070
Neil Patrick Harris made it his mission to
improvise a line that would make Brady crack.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.070
The one that worked?

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:21.140
A reference to a song by Britney Spears' backup
dancer-turned-husband, Kevin Federline.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:21.640
"What?"

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.140
"What?"

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:22.640
"What?"

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:23.140
"Cool."

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:23.640
"Popozao."

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.720
Brady had to quickly duck away to keep from
cracking up on camera — an awkward bit of

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:33.400
blocking, but the end result was too funny
to cut.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.400
The Brady Bunch

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.820
In his 1992 memoir Growing Up Brady, Barry
Williams revealed he taped a scene for the

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:43.610
ultra-innocent family sitcom while completely
stoned.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:47.261
To be fair, he was a young dude in California
in the early '70s, and he thought he had the

00:02:47.261 --> 00:02:48.280
day off.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:53.210
But then he got a call from the producers,
who needed him on set that day after all.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.210
Oops!

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.810
"Far out!"

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:59.910
Somehow nobody associated with The Brady Bunch
thought it was weird that Williams tripped

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:05.080
over his bike pump, awkwardly waved, slurred
his words, or looked the wrong way when his

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:09.520
onscreen little sister arrived on scene, all
with a dopey grin on his face.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.870
Or maybe a secret hero knew what was up, and
decided to leave it in as a gift to future

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:15.340
generations?

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.760
Mystery Science Theater 3000

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.380
This cult classic follows the interstellar
travails of a poor sap imprisoned on a spaceship

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:26.540
with a crew of robots, mocking the low-budget
movies they're forced to watch.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:31.930
Many of the films are riddled with mistakes—so
it's ironic that MST3K had its own spectacular

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.650
blooper make it into the finished product.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.680
Inspired by a weapon in a terrible movie called
Danger!!

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.560
Death Ray, Tom Servo made his own death ray
and fired it at Crow.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:43.220
That was all supposed to happen.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:47.090
"I've gotta admit, it is pretty funny!"

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.990
The Crow puppet, however, wasn't supposed
to catch fire.

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:54.380
It was just the sort of anarchic silliness
that made Mystery Science Theater 3000 so

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.120
special…so the take was used.

